{%- comment -%}
  LBASS — ONE-OF-ONE TEST (2026-08-29). Echoes "1" or "0".

  WHY THIS EXISTS. Every surface in this theme tested uniqueness with

      {% if product.available and product.total_inventory == 1 %}

  and `product.total_inventory` renders EMPTY on this storefront. Measured on
  the live product object for zara-black-chunky-boots-size-39, which the Admin
  API reports as totalInventory:1, tracked, availableForSale:true:

      total_inventory=   avail=true  variants=1
      selv_qty=1  selv_mgmt=shopify  selv_avail=true  selv_policy=deny

  So the comparison was nil == 1 — false for every product, forever. The 1/1
  stamp rendered "LIVE" on all 42 products of the /collections/one-of-one
  collection, the PDP badge never appeared, and the same dead test was copied
  into search, the vault page, the homepage hero and the look card. This was
  invisible because a second bug (.chip{...!important} in lbass-stamp flattening
  the unique chip — see lbass-unique-badge.liquid) meant that even a firing
  badge would have looked like every other chip.

  WHAT IS RELIABLE. variant.inventory_quantity and variant.inventory_management
  both resolve correctly, so uniqueness is summed from the variants instead.

  HONESTY RULE. If ANY variant has no inventory management, units are unknown
  and this returns "0". A "pièce unique" claim on a piece we cannot count is a
  false scarcity claim to the customer — the badge stays off rather than guess.

  USAGE — render returns a string, so capture and strip it:

      {% capture one_s %}{% render 'lbass-one-of-one', product: product %}{% endcapture %}
      {% assign one_s = one_s | strip %}
      {% assign card_one = false %}{% if one_s == '1' %}{% assign card_one = true %}{% endif %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign lb_units = 0
  assign lb_untracked = false
  for v in product.variants
    if v.inventory_management == blank
      assign lb_untracked = true
    endif
    if v.inventory_quantity > 0
      assign lb_units = lb_units | plus: v.inventory_quantity
    endif
  endfor
  if product.available and lb_untracked == false and lb_units == 1
    echo '1'
  else
    echo '0'
  endif
-%}
